  m_Name: Scene12_FAQ_1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::OhmsLaw.DialogueLine
  id: Scene12_FAQ_1
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: Because this nichrome wire always opposes current by the same amount. Push
    it with one volt and you get 0.2 ampere; push it with two volts and you get 0.4
    ampere. Volts divided by amperes comes out at 5 every single time, and that constant
    is the wire's resistance.
  ttsText: Because this nichrome wire always opposes current by the same amount.
    Push it with one volt and you get 0.2 ampere; push it with two volts and you
    get 0.4 ampere. Volts divided by amperes comes out at 5 every single time, and
    that constant is the wire's resistance.
